<title>RUSSIA: Russian current a/c surplus widens in Q3.</title>
<headline>Russian current a/c surplus widens in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's surplus on the current account balance of payments widened to $3.16 billion in the third quarter of this year from $2.44 billion in the second quarter, the Central Bank said in its latest bulletin.</p>
<p>The central bank issued the following balance of payments data (figures in millions of dollars).</p>
<p>    WITH ALL COUNTRIES		Q3 1996    Q2 1996    Q1 1996</p>
<p>    Current account balance	  +3,158     +2,439     +4,646</p>
<p>     Merchandise trade		 +6,262     +5,760     +5,452</p>
<p>	  Exports (FOB)		 +21,583    +21,639    +20,088</p>
<p>	  Imports (FOB)		 -15,320    -15,880    -14,636</p>
<p>     Balance of services	     -1,097     -1,291     -1,309</p>
<p>	  Exports of services	  +2,831     +2,396     +1,992</p>
<p>	  Imports of services	  -3,928     -3,687     -3,301</p>
<p>    Capital transfers balance	  -226	 -248	 -242</p>
<p>    Direct investment balance	  +697	  +69	 +401</p>
<p>     Investment in Russia		+757	 +237	 +436</p>
<p>    Portfolio investment balance     +239	 +750     +1,344</p>
<p>    New government borrowing	 +1,480     +1,516     +4,054</p>
<p>    EXCLUDING FORMER SOVIET UNION Q3 1996    Q2 1996    Q1 1996</p>
<p>    Current account balance	  +3,743     +2,819     +4,528</p>
<p>    Merchandise trade		  +6,758     +6,030     +5,291</p>
<p>	  Exports (FOB)		 +17,415    +17,087    +15,251</p>
<p>	  Imports (FOB)		 -10,656    -11,058     -9,960</p>
<p>NOTES - Government borrowing figures show hard currency only. 1995 data not available.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
